NEMESIS / OPERATOR — FIRST START

Map: https://globe.airplanes.live/
Desktop: KDE Plasma Wayland. The local offline page appears when the remote site cannot be reached.
Wallpapers are launched via /etc/xdg/autostart/nemesis-operator-wallpaper.desktop
The operator launcher only starts in a graphical Wayland session advertising zwlr_layer_shell_v1.
If incompatible, the normal KDE wallpaper remains visible; no forced session changes.

Operator applications are preloaded but do not capture or transmit automatically.
  konsole         Terminal and shell
  gqrx            Interactive SDR receiver (launch only after connecting a supported device)
  rtl_test        Check compatible RTL-SDR receiver (explicit action only)
  dump1090_rs     ADS-B decoder (explicit action, use --help first)
  gpsd            GNSS support (not enabled at boot)
  nmap, tcpdump   Network diagnostics (require authorized scope)
  wg             WireGuard client (no keys or tunnels preinstalled)

The live operator session auto-logins on the *live ISO only* with a locked user
and no sudo privileges or remote SSH listener. Do not store private data in RAM-backed
live media. For a real installation, configure user authentication, storage encryption,
recovery, network and power settings separately.

Wallpaper source: https://github.com/pskeffington/linux_live_wallpaper
License: MIT (bundled at build time) — renderer is built from an exact pinned commit.
Third-party map: airplanes.live, externally hosted, not mirrored or copied into Nemesis.
